# Euler's quadrilateral theorem — the sides' squares exceed the diagonals' squares by four times the square of the segment joining the diagonals' midpoints (source: Euler 1748)
A B C = triangle
D = free
M = midpoint(A, C)
N = midpoint(B, D)
prove dist(A, B) ^ 2 + dist(B, C) ^ 2 + dist(C, D) ^ 2 + dist(D, A) ^ 2 = dist(A, C) ^ 2 + dist(B, D) ^ 2 + 4 * dist(M, N) ^ 2
